Lab 7: Code Coverage and Sonarqube Integration
Areas Covered

Code coverage and Sonarqube.
Sonarqube integration with Jenkins.
Sonarqube Jenkins pipeline to generate code analysis and code coverage report.

Requirements

SonarQube Docker: docker run -d --name sonarqube -p 9000:9000 sonarqube:community.
SonarQube Scanner and SonarQube plugin in Jenkins.
pom.xml with JaCoCo for coverage: <plugin><groupId>org.jacoco</groupId><artifactId>jacoco-maven-plugin</artifactId>...</plugin>.

Plan of Execution and Guidance

SonarQube Setup:
Access http://localhost:9000 > Create project/token.
Production Tip: Use PostgreSQL backend for prod; enable auth with LDAP.
Jenkins Integration:
Install SonarQube Scanner plugin.
Global Config: Add server URL/token.

Pipeline Integration:
Stage: withSonarQubeEnv('SonarQube') { sh 'mvn sonar:sonar' }.
Add Quality Gate: waitForQualityGate abortPipeline: true.
Guidance: Run mvn jacoco:report for coverage; push commit with low coverage to test gate failure.Production Tip: Schedule nightly scans; set gates like "Coverage >80%" for prod branches.

Solution

Expected Outcome: Sonar dashboard shows bugs/duplications/coverage; pipeline aborts on gate fail.
Pipeline Stage:groovystage('Sonar Analysis') {
    steps {
        withSonarQubeEnv('SonarQube') {
            sh 'mvn clean jacoco:prepare-agent test jacoco:report sonar:sonar -Dsonar.projectKey=myapp'
        }
    }
}
stage('Quality Gate') {
    steps {
        timeout(time: 1, unit: 'HOURS') {
            waitForQualityGate abortPipeline: true
        }
    }
}
Verification: Sonar project page: Metrics show coverage % (e.g., 75%); issues list. Pipeline log: "Quality Gate: OK".
Common Issues & Fixes: Token invalid—regenerate. Solution: Check Jenkins credentials store.


